From 4c3f73685807fce19b81324ce50897c68bc5858d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Le=20Goffic?= <legoffic.clement@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:59:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] soc: renesas: rcar-mfis: Clear stale doorbells on channel
 startup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The boot stages talk SCMI over the same MFIS channel as the kernel.
The server answers each of their requests by setting the agent doorbell
bit, and a boot stage that polls the shared memory instead of taking the
interrupt never clears it.
The bit is still set when the kernel requests the channel, so the
interrupt fires the moment request_irq() enables it.
That is before the SCMI mailbox transport has assigned its channel info,
and the receive callback crashes on the NULL pointer from within
mbox_request_channel().

Clear the doorbell before enabling the interrupt so only requests made
by the kernel itself can raise it.

Co-developed-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Clément Le Goffic <clegoffic@baylibre.com>
---
 drivers/soc/renesas/rcar-mfis.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/renesas/rcar-mfis.c b/drivers/soc/renesas/rcar-mfis.c
index 3435c3e16198..9c309ec4f4ca 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/renesas/rcar-mfis.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/renesas/rcar-mfis.c
@@ -108,10 +108,14 @@ static irqreturn_t mfis_mb_iicr_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 static int mfis_mb_startup(struct mbox_chan *chan)
 {
 	struct mfis_chan_priv *chan_priv = chan->con_priv;
+	struct mfis_priv *priv = mfis_mb_mbox_to_priv(chan->mbox);
 
 	if (!chan_priv->irq)
 		return 0;
 
+	/* A doorbell left set by a boot stage fires before the client is ready */
+	mfis_write(&priv->mbox_reg, chan_priv->reg, 0);
+
 	return request_irq(chan_priv->irq, mfis_mb_iicr_interrupt, 0,
 			   dev_name(chan->mbox->dev), chan);
 }
